// The same beat inserted by two beats sees the local state of the beat that
// inserts it: name resolution walks the stack of the moment. A persistent beat
// state, a temporary `new state` and a parameter all shadow the same way, and a
// parameter can change from one pick to the next.

beat Start
  Calm()
  Angry()
  Calm()
  Fresh()
  Fresh()
  Named("soft")
  Named("loud")
  Named("soft")

beat Calm
  state
    tone: "calm"
  when
    + Mood
    true
      Calm fallback.

beat Angry
  state
    tone: "angry"
  when
    + Mood
    true
      Angry fallback.

beat Fresh
  new state
    tone: "fresh"
  when
    + Mood
    true
      Fresh fallback.

beat Named(tone)
  when
    + Mood
    true
      Named fallback.

beat Mood
  when
    tone is "calm"
      A calm word.
    tone is "angry"
      An angry word.
    tone is "fresh"
      A fresh word.
    tone is "soft"
      A soft word.
    tone is "loud"
      A loud word.

/*
<test>
- expected: |
    ~ A calm word.

    ~ An angry word.

    ~ A calm word.

    ~ A fresh word.

    ~ A fresh word.

    ~ A soft word.

    ~ A loud word.

    ~ A soft word.
</test>
*/
